# Code formatting and typing

- Prefer the existing project formatter (Prettier/eslint) for indentation, spacing, and quotes.
- Do not introduce manual visual alignment or decorative spacing; let the formatter decide.
- Keep files cohesive and focused; extract helpers when functions/components become large or do many things.

## Type vs interface

- Use `type` aliases instead of `interface` for new structural definitions in TypeScript and Vue script blocks.
- Do not add new `interface` declarations in this project.
- When touching code that already uses `interface`, prefer refactoring to `type` if it is practical and low-risk.

```typescript
// ❌ Avoid
interface UserProps {
  id: number;
  name: string;
}

// ✅ Prefer
type UserProps = {
  id: number;
  name: string;
};
```

## Exact and precise types

- Avoid overly broad types such as `any`, `unknown`, `object`, `{ [key: string]: any }`, or `Record<string, any>` when a more precise type is possible.
- Prefer exact object shapes, string literal unions, and discriminated unions instead of loose index signatures.
- Give exported functions, composables, and Vue component props/emit definitions explicit parameter and return types.
- Model nullability and optionality explicitly with unions like `Foo | null` or `Foo | undefined`.

```typescript
// ❌ Avoid
type ApiResponse = any;

// ✅ Prefer
type ApiStatus = "idle" | "loading" | "success" | "error";

type ApiResponse =
  | { status: "success"; data: Movie[] }
  | { status: "error"; message: string };
```

## ESLint usage

- Do not use `// eslint-disable`, `// eslint-disable-next-line`, or similar directives in new or modified code.
- If a lint rule is too strict, change the implementation or adjust the shared eslint configuration instead of disabling it locally.

```typescript
// ❌ Avoid
// eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
function handleEvent(payload: any) {
  /* ... */
}

// ✅ Prefer
type EventPayload = {
  type: "click" | "submit";
  targetId: string;
};

function handleEvent(payload: EventPayload) {
  /* ... */
}
```
